# Small pawnless endings for testing the pawnless_endings switch: FEN ; the ending, the
# stronger side, the side to move, and the tablebase's DTZ for a win (from the side to move's
# view, so negative when it loses) or else its result.
#
# 100 positions of four and five men in which each side has a piece and nobody has a pawn:
# the endings the switch hands to the hand-crafted evaluation. The pieces were placed at random
# (legal, nobody in check) and each position was looked up in the Lichess tablebase API
# (tablebase.lichess.ovh) on 2026-10-26. The queen endings, against a rook, a bishop or a
# knight, are all wins for the queen under the fifty-move rule, at least ten plies from the
# win. The others are kept whatever their result, mostly draws, to show the switch does no harm
# there. Each position is played twice in a match, once with each engine on the stronger side.
#
